      "id": "s2",
      "description": "Identify the three radiator candidates from candidate_specs.md and extract their key properties (refractive index, transparency, ageing characteristics) to determine which candidates meet the hard requirement of <10% transparency loss after 10-year humidity ageing."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "description": "For each radiator candidate that passes the ageing requirement, use the simulation tool to calculate pion/kaon separation performance at 10 GeV/c for different thicknesses (systematically test values between 1-6 cm, e.g., 2, 3, 4, 5 cm) and record the results."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "description": "Analyze the recorded simulation results to identify which radiator-thickness combinations achieve the minimum 3.5 sigma pion/kaon separation requirement at 10 GeV/c."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "description": "Among the combinations that meet both hard requirements (≥3.5 sigma separation and <10% transparency loss), identify the optimal radiator and thickness that provides the best pion/kaon separation performance."
    }
  ]
}
